{"name":"Amazon Parrot","hex":"#80e45f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"amazon parrot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A New World parrot of the genus Amazona."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amazon_parrot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Amazon parrot","blocks":[{"text":"Amazon parrots are parrots in the genus Amazona. They are medium-sized, short-tailed parrots native to the Americas, with their range extending from South America to Mexico and the Caribbean. Amazona is one of the 92 genera of parrots that make up the order Psittaciformes and are in the family Psittacidae, one of three families of true parrots. It contains about 30 species. Most amazons are predominantly green, with accenting colors that depend on the species, and they can be quite vivid. They feed primarily on seeds, nuts, and fruits, supplemented by leafy matter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Amazona_parrots_collage.jpg/330px-Amazona_parrots_collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_parrot","wikidata":"Q456513"},{"title":"Parrot","blocks":[{"text":"Parrots, also known as psittacines from the name of the type genus Psittacus, are birds with a strong curved beak, upright stance, and clawed feet. They are classified in four families that contain roughly 410 species in 101 genera, found mostly in tropical and subtropical regions. The four families are the Psittaculidae, Psittacidae, Cacatuidae (cockatoos), and Strigopidae. One-third of all parrot species are threatened by extinction, with a higher aggregate extinction risk than any other comparable bird group. Parrots have a generally pantropical distribution with several species inhabiting temperate regions as well. The greatest diversity of parrots is in South America and Australasia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Rainbow_lorikeet_%28Trichoglossus_moluccanus_moluccanus%29_Sydney.jpg/330px-Rainbow_lorikeet_%28Trichoglossus_moluccanus_moluccanus%29_Sydney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parrot","wikidata":"Q31431"},{"title":"Jungle green","blocks":[{"text":"Jungle green is a color that is a rich tone of medium spring green."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle_green","wikidata":"Q373658"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/ChrysotisChloronotaKeulemans.jpg/500px-ChrysotisChloronotaKeulemans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/ChrysotisChloronotaKeulemans.jpg/500px-ChrysotisChloronotaKeulemans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChrysotisChloronotaKeulemans.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Jamaican_parrot.jpg/500px-Jamaican_parrot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Jamaican_parrot.jpg/500px-Jamaican_parrot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJamaican_parrot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Red-lored_parrot_%28Amazona_autumnalis_salvini%29_feeding.jpg/250px-Red-lored_parrot_%28Amazona_autumnalis_salvini%29_feeding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Red-lored_parrot_%28Amazona_autumnalis_salvini%29_feeding.jpg/500px-Red-lored_parrot_%28Amazona_autumnalis_salvini%29_feeding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/